# The MCP image's build context.
#
# This image is built from the repository root (`docker build -f mcp/Dockerfile .`)
# because it needs the browser app's engine sources, so it cannot use
# mcp/.dockerignore - that one only applies when mcp/ is itself the context.
#
# BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the root
# .dockerignore, which is what keeps this image's context independent of the
# app image's. Without it both images share one ignore file, and an exclusion
# added for one silently empties the other - the app image's `mcp` exclusion
# did exactly that, and the MCP build failed with "/mcp/src: not found".
